---
scope: "The CONTENT of the bootstrap primer: the four live families every spawned Intelligence fetches at wake — `bootstrap-core` (discipline, unconditional), the HOST axis `bootstrap-ic` and `bootstrap-terminal`, and the DOMAIN axis `bootstrap-cp`. Each member is a routing card carrying a way of reasoning or a pointer at a live surface, never a copy of one. Authored 2026-08-14 against the ratified contract in [SPEC:CXC-GRAPH-PRIMER]."
audience: "Every Intelligence at wake — this is the document its bootstrap queries return. Also whoever adds a member later, and the architect ratifying the split."
boundary: "IN: the member text of the four LIVE families, each carrying its `function` membership value, its `primer-order`, and — for every scoped member — the `authority` pointer that outranks it. OUT: the governing contract itself (membership predicate, query shape, budget, invariants, toolbox disposition, prompt wiring) which lives in [SPEC:CXC-GRAPH-PRIMER] and is deliberately not restated here; the reserved-but-not-live family names; and every capability inventory, which is a pointer's job."
not-this: "Not a specification — it specifies nothing and is governed rather than governing. Not a capability manifest: no member states what any named agent, service or harness CAN or CANNOT do. Not a copy of `bootstrap/toolbox.md`: the sections that moved were moved under that spec's disposition, the version-pinned and per-agent-capability sections were dropped, and the role-specific ones were relocated."
domain: plt.cio
confidentiality: internal-only
artifact-readiness: system-design
